      <div class="space-y-8 text-text-main leading-relaxed">
        <h2>1. Combined Prelims Exam Pattern (100 Marks)</h2>
        <p>
          The Preliminary examination is common for both Group B and Group C posts. It serves as a screening test to qualify candidates for the Mains exam.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li><strong><u>Total Questions:</u></strong> 100 Multiple Choice Questions (MCQs).</li>
          <li><strong><u>Total Marks:</u></strong> 100 Marks.</li>
          <li><strong><u>Duration:</u></strong> 1 Hour (60 Minutes).</li>
          <li><strong><u>Negative Marking:</u></strong> 1/4th (25%) deduction for every incorrect answer.</li>
          <li><strong><u>Subjects Covered:</u></strong> Current Affairs, Civics/Polity, History of India & Maharashtra, Geography of India & Maharashtra, Indian Economy & Budget, General Science (Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Hygiene), Aptitude & Logical Reasoning.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Mains Exam Pattern (400 Marks)</h2>
        <p>
          The Mains examination consists of 2 papers of 200 marks each (Total 400 Marks):
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li><strong><u>Paper 1 (Languages - 200 Marks):</u></strong> 50 Questions on Marathi (12th Std Standard - 100 Marks) and 50 Questions on English (Degree Standard - 100 Marks). Duration: 1 Hour.</li>
          <li><strong><u>Paper 2 (General Ability Test & Post Knowledge - 200 Marks):</u></strong> 100 Questions covering General Knowledge, Reasoning, Computer & IT, RTI Act 2005, Maharashtra Public Services Rights Act 2015, and Post-Specific Technical Concepts (Clerk, Tax Assistant, Excise). Duration: 1 Hour.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Computer Typing Skill Test</h2>
        <p>
          Candidates qualifying for Clerk-Typist and Tax Assistant posts must clear the Desktop Typing Skill Test (Qualifying nature):
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li><strong><u>Clerk Typist:</u></strong> Marathi 30 WPM or English 40 WPM certificate & skill test.</li>
          <li><strong><u>Tax Assistant:</u></strong> Marathi 30 WPM <strong><u>and</u></strong> English 40 WPM certificate & skill test.</li>
        </ul>
